{"question_text": {"স্পেশাল বিসিএস (স্বাস্থ্য) - লং কোর্স": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Cholecystokinin is secreted from-", "option1": "D cells", "option2": "I cells", "option3": "K cells", "option4": "L cells", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1953.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Condition where colonoscopy is not useful-", "option1": "Chronic diarrhoea ", "option2": "Constipation ", "option3": "Rectal bleeding ", "option4": "Altered bowel habit", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1955.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Which is not an alarm feature of dyspepsia?", "option1": "Anaemia ", "option2": "Age over 55 years", "option3": "Haematemesis", "option4": "Palpable abdominal mass", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1957.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Amount of fluid excreted daily in stools-", "option1": "100 ml", "option2": "150 ml", "option3": "200 ml", "option4": "300 ml", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1954.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) Which one is a feature of chronic small bowel diarrhoea-", "option1": "Steatorrhoea", "option2": "Undigested food in stool", "option3": "Large volume, watery stool ", "option4": "Blood and mucus in stool", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1959.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Acrodermatitis enteropathica is a consequence of which nutrient malabsorption?", "option1": "Vitamin A", "option2": "Vitamin C ", "option3": "Zinc", "option4": "Magnesium ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1960.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Which of the following act as the Pacemaker of the gut?", "option1": "Migrating motor complexes", "option2": "Enterochromaffin like cells", "option3": "Interstitial cells of Cajal", "option4": "Paneth cells", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><u><strong>Peristalsis</strong></u><br /><br />Peristalsis is a reflex triggered by gut wall distension, which consists of a wave of circular muscle contraction to propel contents from the oesophagus to the rectum. It can be influenced by innervation but functions independently. It results from a basic electrical rhythm originating from the <strong>interstitial cells of Cajal</strong> in the circular layer of intestinal smooth muscle. These are stellate cells of mesenchymal origin with smooth muscle features, which act as the <strong>&lsquo;pacemaker&rsquo; of the gut.</strong></p>"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) Which test is used to asses pancreatic exocrine function?", "option1": "Faecal elastase", "option2": "Faecal calprotectin", "option3": "75SeHCAT test", "option4": "S. Amylase", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1956_n3gSxrS.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Helicobacter pylori testing is not indicated in-", "option1": "Past history of PUD", "option2": "ITP", "option3": "Unexplained Vitamin B12 deficiency ", "option4": "Gastro-oesophageal reflux disease ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1961.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Which of the following is an example of bulk forming laxative?", "option1": "Lactulose", "option2": "Magnesium salts", "option3": "Senna", "option4": "Methyl cellulose ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1962.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Which of the following is true for Ulcerative colitis?", "option1": "More common in non smokers", "option2": "Skip lesions", "option3": "Deep fissuring ulcers", "option4": "Slight female predominance ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1963.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Which of the following drugs is safe for treatment of IBD during pregnancy?", "option1": "Methotrexate ", "option2": "Tofacitinib", "option3": "Azathioprine", "option4": "Ciclosporin", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1966.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) Glasgow criteria for prognosis of acute pancreatitis include-", "option1": "Age <55 yeras", "option2": "Serum calcium >2 mmol/L", "option3": "Glucose > 10 mmol/L", "option4": "Albumin <3.2 g/L", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1967.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) Successful eradication of H. Pylori can be confirmed by-", "option1": "Rapid urease test", "option2": "Microbiological culture", "option3": "Urea breath test", "option4": "Lactose H2 breath test", "answer": "3", "exp": "<strong>Davidson 24th Ed. Page: 799<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1958.jpg\" alt=\"\" /></strong>"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) Histological feature of Crohn’s disease is?", "option1": "Inflammation is confined to the mucosa", "option2": "Loss of goblet cells", "option3": "Non caseating granuloma", "option4": "Crypt abscesses", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1964.jpg\" alt=\"\" /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1965.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) Cause of chronic pancreatitis-", "option1": "Gallstones", "option2": "Post ERCP", "option3": "Sphincter of Oddi stenosis", "option4": "Sphincter of Oddi dysfunction ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<strong>Sphincter of Oddi dysfunction is a cause of Acute pancreatitis.</strong><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1968.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) Test used to demonstrate anatomy of pancreas prior to surgery-", "option1": "Ultrasound ", "option2": "MRCP", "option3": "Computed tomography ", "option4": "Endoscopic ultrasound ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1969.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Which one is a sign of decompression in hepatic cirrhosis?", "option1": "Splenomegaly ", "option2": "Dilated abdominal wall veins", "option3": "Bruising ", "option4": "Flapping tremor", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1970.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) The functional unit of liver is-", "option1": "Hepatocyte", "option2": "Hepatic acinus", "option3": "Hepatic lobule", "option4": "Sinusoids", "answer": "2", "exp": "<strong>Davidson 24th Ed. Page 862<br /><br /></strong><sup><em>A liver segment is made up of multiple smaller units known as lobules, comprised of a central vein, radiating sinusoids separated from each other by single liver cell (hepatocyte) plates, and peripheral portal tracts containing terminal branches of the hepatic artery, portal vein and bile duct.</em></sup><strong><sup><em> The functional unit of the liver is the hepatic acinus.</em></sup><br /></strong>"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Which cell play a key role in the development of hepatic fibrosis?", "option1": "Hepatocytes", "option2": "NK cells", "option3": "Stellate cell", "option4": "Sinusoidal endothelial cell", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1972.jpg\" alt=\"\" /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1971.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) Initial test for Haemochromatosis?", "option1": "Liver biopsy ", "option2": "Transferrin Saturation ", "option3": "HFE gene test", "option4": "Liver function tests", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1973.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) Which of the following causes fluctuating jaundice?", "option1": "Ampullary tumour ", "option2": "Primary biliary cholangitis", "option3": "Choledocholithiasis", "option4": "Pancreatic pseudocyst", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1974.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) Most common cause of acute liver failure is?", "option1": "Paracetamol toxicity ", "option2": "Anti tuberculous drugs", "option3": "Acute viral hepatitis ", "option4": "Cryptogenic acute liver failure ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<strong>Davidson 24th Ed. Page 873.<br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1975.jpg\" alt=\"\" /></strong>"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) Best screening test for acute Hepatitis B infection is?", "option1": "HBsAg", "option2": "Hepatitis B core IgM antibody ", "option3": "Anti HBs", "option4": "HBeAg", "answer": "2", "exp": "<strong>Davidson 24th Ed, Page 874<br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1976.jpg\" alt=\"\" /><br /></strong>"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) Cause of high SAAG ascites?", "option1": "Nephrotic syndrome", "option2": "Meigs syndrome ", "option3": "Protein losing enteropathy", "option4": "Cirrhosis ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1977.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) Which of the following does not precipitate hepatic encephalopathy?", "option1": "Dehydration ", "option2": "Gastrointestinal bleeding ", "option3": "Hypocalcaemia", "option4": "Constipation ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1978.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) Cardinal feature of portal hypertension is?", "option1": "Palmar erythema", "option2": "Splenomegaly ", "option3": "Ascites", "option4": "Hepatomegaly ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<strong>Davidson 24th Ed. Page 881<br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1979.jpg\" alt=\"\" /></strong>"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) Which of the following is a DNA virus?", "option1": "Hepatitis A virus", "option2": "Hepatitis B virus", "option3": "Hepatitis C virus", "option4": "Hepatitis E virus", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1980.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) Drug causing cholestatic hepatitis?", "option1": "Rifampicin", "option2": "Isoniazid ", "option3": "NSAIDs", "option4": "Amiodarone", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1981.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) In autoimmune hepatitis, there is a high serum levels of which immunoglobulin?", "option1": "IgA", "option2": "IgM", "option3": "IgG", "option4": "IgE", "answer": "3", "exp": "<strong>Davidson 24th Ed. Page 897</strong><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1982.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "31", "question": "৩১) Which serological marker for hepatitis B virus infection will be positive in a previously immunised individual?", "option1": "HBsAg", "option2": "Anti HBs", "option3": "Anti HBc IgM", "option4": "Anti HBc IgG", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1984.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "32", "question": "৩২) Adverse prognostic criteria in acute liver failure due to paracetamol overdose?", "option1": "pH > 7.25", "option2": "Prothrombin time < 100 seconds", "option3": "Prothrombin time > 100 seconds ", "option4": "Bilirubin >300 micromol/L", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1985.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "33", "question": "৩৩) Gold standard investigation for Coeliac disease is?", "option1": "Anti endomysial antibody", "option2": "Anti tTG antibody", "option3": "Full blood count", "option4": "Endoscopic small bowel biopsy ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1986.jpg\" alt=\"\" /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1987.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "34", "question": "৩৪) Non invasive test for H. Pylori?", "option1": "Microbiological culture ", "option2": "Serology ", "option3": "Histology ", "option4": "Rapid urease test", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1988.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "35", "question": "৩৫) Which one of the following is a feature of Primary sclerosing cholangitis?", "option1": "Occurs in younger age", "option2": "Associated with autoimmune thyroid disease ", "option3": "Predominantly intrahepatic bile duct injury", "option4": "AMA+ve in 90% cases", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1989.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1128\" height=\"1000\" />"}, {"id": "36", "question": "৩৬) Which of the following is not stored in liver?", "option1": "Vitamin A", "option2": "Vitamin D", "option3": "Iron", "option4": "Bilirubin ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1990.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "37", "question": "৩৭) Which of the following decreases gastric acid secretion?", "option1": "Gastrin", "option2": "Secretin", "option3": "Ghrelin", "option4": "Vasoactive intestinal peptide", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1953_SaoFA6z.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "38", "question": "৩৮) Which of the following acts as a stimulus for secretion of Ghrelin?", "option1": "Fatty acids", "option2": "Feeding", "option3": "Fasting", "option4": "Product of of protein digestion ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1953_53m3ewA.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "39", "question": "৩৯) Relative contraindication of upper GI endoscopy is?", "option1": "Recent myocardial infarction ", "option2": "Severe shock", "option3": "Severe respiratory disease ", "option4": "Possible visceral perforation ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1991.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "40", "question": "৪০) Milky-white ascitic fluid can be found in?", "option1": "Infection ", "option2": "Cirrhosis ", "option3": "Malignant disease ", "option4": "Lymphatic obstruction ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_1993.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}]}, "_source": "archive-question-subject", "_exam_id": 6109, "custom_field": "প্রতি প্রশ্নের মান ১ ও ভুল উত্তরের জন্য ০.৫০ কাটা যাবে।", "exam_time": "1200000", "is_omr": false, "omr_time": "7200000", "examname": "May 29, 2024", "type": "BCS-Health-Long", "payment": "BALANCE_NOT"}